        12,
        13
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.mckinneytexas.org/122/History",
      "category": "people",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "When the Houston and Texas Central Railroad reached McKinney in 1872, the town became Collin County's commercial hub.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        20,
        21,
        24
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/McKinney%2C_Texas",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The Collin County History Museum, housed in the 1911 post office, offers free admission several days a week.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        7
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/McKinney%2C_Texas",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "McKinney's downtown showcases 19th‑century limestone storefronts and Victorian architecture, setting the scene for many annual events.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        15,
        25
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://authentictexas.com/destinations/mckinney/",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
